IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sgc2-common`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 6 Division 2, section 209 (the auditor's duties to the trustee for debenture holders), section 209A (interpretation of the Part) and section 209B
-- (repealed: no function). LAYER 1 (the law, objectively).
--
-- The Accounting Standards are not among the sources. Where section 209A says a term "has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards", the function takes the Standards'
-- answer as a plain fact and answers JUST TRUE where it is given, NOTHING where it is not (the text points outside its sources). Where it says a term "means" something defined partly by
-- the Standards ("means a company that is required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in relation to a group"), the Standards' part is a plain fact and the
-- definition is closed: JUST TRUE where the whole description is met, JUST FALSE where it is not (a "means" definition).

§ `The acts and parties of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 209 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 209(1) send by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the borrowing corporation a copy of the financial statements or of the report, certificate or other document`
    `s 209(2) send by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee`

§ `Section 209: the auditor's duties to the trustee for debenture holders`

-- (1): "The auditor of a borrowing corporation must within 7 days after furnishing the corporation with any financial statements or any report, certificate or other document which the auditor is required by this Act
-- or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the corporation, send by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the borrowing corporation a copy thereof."
-- "within 7 days after furnishing": the day of furnishing is not counted, so the last day is the day of furnishing plus 7 days (P1).
-- src:20101 | 209.—(1) The auditor of a borrowing corporation must within
-- src:20102 | 7 days after furnishing the corporation with any financial statements
-- src:20103 | or any report, certificate or other document which the auditor is
-- src:20104 | required by this Act or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the
-- src:20105 | corporation, send by post to every trustee for the holders of
-- src:20106 | debentures of the borrowing corporation a copy thereof.
@ref s 209(1) (src:20101-20106)
GIVEN `the day the auditor furnished the corporation with the financial statements or the report, certificate or other document` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 209(1) the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the auditor furnished the corporation with the financial statements or the report, certificate or other document` 7 Days

@ref s 209(1) (src:20101-20106)
GIVEN `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has furnished the corporation with financial statements or a report, certificate or other document which the auditor is required by this Act or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the auditor furnished it` IS A DATE
      `the auditor has sent by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation a copy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the copy was sent` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(1) the auditor is in default of the duty to send a copy to every trustee` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation is a borrowing corporation`
       AND `the auditor has furnished the corporation with financial statements or a report, certificate or other document which the auditor is required by this Act or by the debentures or trust deed to give to the corporation`
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the auditor has sent by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation a copy`
              `the day the copy was sent`
              (`s 209(1) the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee` `the day the auditor furnished it`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The auditor of a borrowing corporation must within 7 days after furnishing the corporation with any financial statements or any report, certificate or other document ..., send by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the borrowing corporation a copy thereof" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or not engaged: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 209(1) (src:20101-20106)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the day the auditor furnished it` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 209 act`
`s 209(1) the auditor must send a copy to every trustee within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 209(1) send by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures of the borrowing corporation a copy of the financial statements or of the report, certificate or other document`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the auditor furnished it` (`s 209(1) the last day for the auditor to send a copy to every trustee` `the day the auditor furnished it`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not send by post to every trustee for the holders of debentures a copy within 7 days after furnishing the borrowing corporation with the document"

-- (2): "Where, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of a borrowing corporation, the auditor becomes aware of any matter which is in the auditor's opinion relevant to the exercise and performance of
-- the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation, the auditor must, within 7 days after so becoming aware of the matter, send by post
-- a report in writing on such matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy thereof to the trustee."
-- src:20110 | (2) Where, in the performance of the auditor’s duties as auditor of a
-- src:20111 | borrowing corporation, the auditor becomes aware of any matter
-- src:20112 | which is in the auditor’s opinion relevant to the exercise and
-- src:20113 | performance of the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any
-- src:20114 | trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the
-- src:20115 | corporation, the auditor must, within 7 days after so becoming aware
-- src:20116 | of the matter, send by post a report in writing on such matter to the
-- src:20117 | borrowing corporation and a copy thereof to the trustee.
@ref s 209(2) (src:20110-20117)
GIVEN `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 209(2) the last day for the auditor to send the report` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` 7 Days

@ref s 209(2) (src:20110-20117)
GIVEN `the corporation is a borrowing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor has become aware, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of the borrowing corporation, of a matter which is in the auditor's opinion relevant to the exercise and performance of the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` IS A DATE
      `the auditor has sent by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the report and the copy were sent` IS A DATE
      `the day as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(2) the auditor is in default of the duty to send the report` MEANS
    IF     `the corporation is a borrowing corporation`
       AND `the auditor has become aware, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of the borrowing corporation, of a matter which is in the auditor's opinion relevant to the exercise and performance of the powers and duties imposed by this Act or by any trust deed upon any trustee for the holders of debentures of the corporation`
       AND `s 205 helper: default in an act due by the last day`
              `the auditor has sent by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee`
              `the day the report and the copy were sent`
              (`s 209(2) the last day for the auditor to send the report` `the day the auditor became aware of the matter`)
              `the day as at which the question is asked`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where, in the performance of the auditor's duties as auditor of a borrowing corporation, the auditor becomes aware of any matter ..., the auditor must, within 7 days after so becoming aware of the matter, send by post a report in writing on such matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy thereof to the trustee" (a duty met in time, or not yet due, or not engaged: the provision's own question; fork line F-D1)

@ref s 209(2) (src:20110-20117)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
      `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 209 act`
`s 209(2) the auditor must send the report within 7 days` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 209(2) send by post a report in writing on the matter to the borrowing corporation and a copy of it to the trustee`
    WITHIN `s 205 helper: the days from the event to the last day` `the day the auditor became aware of the matter` (`s 209(2) the last day for the auditor to send the report` `the day the auditor became aware of the matter`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not send by post the report in writing to the borrowing corporation and a copy to the trustee within 7 days after becoming aware of the matter"

-- (3): "If any person fails to comply with subsection (2), the person shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty."
-- An unmet element of the offence: JUST FALSE (split site (i), fork line F-E1).
-- src:20119 | (3) If any person fails to comply with subsection (2), the person
-- src:20120 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:20121 | not exceeding $1,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 209(3) (src:20119-20121)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(3) the person is guilty of the offence` MEANS
    IF `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If any person fails to comply with subsection (2)" (an unmet element of the offence: split site (i), fork line F-E1)

@ref s 209(3) (src:20119-20121)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 209(3) the most the person may be fined on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 209(3) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST 1000
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for a person who fails to comply with subsection (2)

-- "and also to a default penalty": the penalty is the one section 408 provides (s 4(1) "default penalty"); its amount is not among the sources.
@ref s 209(3) (src:20119-20121)
GIVEN `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209(3) the person is also liable on conviction to a default penalty` MEANS
    IF `s 209(3) the person is guilty of the offence` `the person fails to comply with subsection (2)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection adds a default penalty only for a person who is guilty of the offence

§ `Section 209A: interpretation of this Part`

-- "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears": the definitions that follow apply unless it does. An "unless" the text introduces: JUST FALSE when the contrary intention appears.
-- src:20125 | 209A. In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears —
@ref s 209A (src:20125-20125)
GIVEN `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A the definitions of this section apply in this Part` MEANS
    IF NOT `a contrary intention appears`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears -- " (an "unless": the contrary intention appears)

-- "balance sheet", in relation to a company, means the balance sheet, by whatever name called, prepared in accordance with the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20127 | “balance sheet”, in relation to a company, means the balance
-- src:20128 | sheet, by whatever name called, prepared in accordance with
-- src:20129 | the Accounting Standards;
@ref s 209A "balance sheet" (src:20127-20129)
GIVEN `the document is the balance sheet of the company, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prepared in accordance with the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "balance sheet" the document is a balance sheet of the company` MEANS
    IF `the document is the balance sheet of the company, by whatever name called` AND `it is prepared in accordance with the Accounting Standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'balance sheet', in relation to a company, means the balance sheet, by whatever name called, prepared in accordance with the Accounting Standards" (a "means" definition)

-- "consolidated financial statements" has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20131 | “consolidated financial statements” has the meaning given by
-- src:20132 | the Accounting Standards;
@ref s 209A "consolidated financial statements" (src:20131-20132)
GIVEN `the Accounting Standards give the statements the meaning of consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "consolidated financial statements" the statements are consolidated financial statements` MEANS
    IF `the Accounting Standards give the statements the meaning of consolidated financial statements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "'consolidated financial statements' has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards", which are not among the sources

-- "consolidated total assets" -- (a) in the case where consolidated financial statements are prepared in relation to a group, are determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group;
-- or (b) in the case where consolidated financial statements are not prepared in relation to a group, means the aggregate total assets of all the members of the group.
-- Limb (a) is a figure determined under standards that are not among the sources: it is supplied. Limb (b) is the sum of the members' total assets.
-- src:20137 | “consolidated total assets” —
-- src:20139 | (a) in the case where consolidated financial statements
-- src:20140 | are prepared in relation to a group — are determined
-- src:20141 | in accordance with the accounting standards
-- src:20142 | applicable to the group; or
-- src:20144 | (b) in the case where consolidated financial statements
-- src:20145 | are not prepared in relation to a group — means the
-- src:20146 | aggregate total assets of all the members of the group;
@ref s 209A "consolidated total assets" (src:20137-20146)
GIVEN `consolidated financial statements are prepared in relation to the group` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consolidated total assets of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the total assets of each of the members of the group, in Singapore dollars` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 209A "consolidated total assets" the consolidated total assets of the group, in Singapore dollars` MEANS
    IF `consolidated financial statements are prepared in relation to the group`
    THEN JUST `the consolidated total assets of the group determined in accordance with the accounting standards applicable to the group, in Singapore dollars`
    ELSE JUST (sum `the total assets of each of the members of the group, in Singapore dollars`)

-- "directors' statement" means the statement of the directors mentioned in section 201(16).
-- src:20148 | “directors’ statement” means the statement of the directors
-- src:20149 | mentioned in section 201(16);
@ref s 209A "directors' statement" (src:20148-20149)
GIVEN `the statement is the statement of the directors mentioned in section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "directors' statement" the statement is the directors' statement` MEANS
    IF `the statement is the statement of the directors mentioned in section 201(16)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'directors' statement' means the statement of the directors mentioned in section 201(16)" (a "means" definition)

-- "entity" means an entity that is referred to in the Accounting Standards in relation to the preparation of financial statements and the requirements for the preparation of financial statements.
-- src:20151 | “entity” means an entity that is referred to in the Accounting
-- src:20152 | Standards in relation to the preparation of financial
-- src:20153 | statements and the requirements for the preparation of
-- src:20154 | financial statements;
@ref s 209A "entity" (src:20151-20154)
GIVEN `the Accounting Standards refer to it as an entity in relation to the preparation of financial statements and the requirements for the preparation of financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "entity" the body is an entity` MEANS
    IF `the Accounting Standards refer to it as an entity in relation to the preparation of financial statements and the requirements for the preparation of financial statements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'entity' means an entity that is referred to in the Accounting Standards in relation to the preparation of financial statements and the requirements for the preparation of financial statements" (a "means" definition)

-- "financial statements" means the financial statements of a company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20156 | “financial statements” means the financial statements of a
-- src:20157 | company required to be prepared by the Accounting
-- src:20158 | Standards;
@ref s 209A "financial statements" (src:20156-20158)
GIVEN `they are the financial statements of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "financial statements" the statements are financial statements` MEANS
    IF `they are the financial statements of a company` AND `they are required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'financial statements' means the financial statements of a company required to be prepared by the Accounting Standards" (a "means" definition)

-- "group" has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20160 | “group” has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards;
@ref s 209A "group" (src:20160-20160)
GIVEN `the Accounting Standards give the arrangement the meaning of a group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "group" the arrangement is a group` MEANS
    IF `the Accounting Standards give the arrangement the meaning of a group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "'group' has the meaning given by the Accounting Standards", which are not among the sources

-- "parent company" means a company that is required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in relation to a group.
-- src:20162 | “parent company” means a company that is required under the
-- src:20163 | Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in
-- src:20164 | relation to a group;
@ref s 209A "parent company" (src:20162-20164)
GIVEN `it is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in relation to a group` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "parent company" the company is a parent company` MEANS
    IF `it is a company` AND `it is required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in relation to a group`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'parent company' means a company that is required under the Accounting Standards to prepare financial statements in relation to a group" (a "means" definition)

-- "subsidiary company" means a company that is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20166 | “subsidiary company” means a company that is a subsidiary as
-- src:20167 | defined in the Accounting Standards;
@ref s 209A "subsidiary company" (src:20166-20167)
GIVEN `it is a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "subsidiary company" the company is a subsidiary company` MEANS
    IF `it is a company` AND `it is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'subsidiary company' means a company that is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards" (a "means" definition)

-- "subsidiary corporation" means a corporation that is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20169 | “subsidiary corporation” means a corporation that is a subsidiary
-- src:20170 | as defined in the Accounting Standards;
@ref s 209A "subsidiary corporation" (src:20169-20170)
GIVEN `it is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "subsidiary corporation" the corporation is a subsidiary corporation` MEANS
    IF `it is a corporation` AND `it is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'subsidiary corporation' means a corporation that is a subsidiary as defined in the Accounting Standards" (a "means" definition)

-- "ultimate parent corporation" means a corporation which is a parent but is not a subsidiary, within the meaning of the Accounting Standards.
-- src:20172 | “ultimate parent corporation” means a corporation which is a
-- src:20173 | parent but is not a subsidiary, within the meaning of the
-- src:20174 | Accounting Standards.
@ref s 209A "ultimate parent corporation" (src:20172-20174)
GIVEN `it is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a parent within the meaning of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a subsidiary within the meaning of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 209A "ultimate parent corporation" the corporation is an ultimate parent corporation` MEANS
    IF `it is a corporation` AND `it is a parent within the meaning of the Accounting Standards` AND (NOT `it is a subsidiary within the meaning of the Accounting Standards`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "'ultimate parent corporation' means a corporation which is a parent but is not a subsidiary, within the meaning of the Accounting Standards" (a "means" definition)
